journey
  title A reader's path through Nooreign — land, read, convene, audit, disagree
  section Arrive
    Land on the atlas: / : 4 : A reader lands on the landing page and sees the numbers: 12 kingdoms, 28 advisors, 32 eras, 20 dilemmas.
    Read the pitch, not the slogan : 5 : The landing page says every verdict is computed locally from axiom vectors, with no API keys.
  section Pick a realm
    Open the realms: /kingdoms : 4 : The grid shows terrain, crest, founder date and each court's one-line AI stance.
    Enter a kingdom: /kingdoms/kantian-citadel : 5 : Creed, motto, axioms, landmarks, relations, canon texts, and its own dilemmas.
  section Read the doctrine
    Meet the bench: /court/kant : 5 : Signature move, works, temperament, six-axis radar, and every argument move the engine can use.
    Check the attribution : 4 : Four moves, each with a claim and a support the reader can verify against the primary text.
  section Convene a court
    Pick a case: /dilemmas/paperclip-maximiser : 4 : Four options, their six deltas, the stakeholders and their welfare weights.
    Sit the court: /council : 5 : Choose advisors, seed and rounds. runCouncil() returns a verdict and a full trace.
    Compare the courts: /council : 4 : compareCouncils() runs one court per kingdom and reports how many distinct verdicts there were.
  section Audit
    Read the trace : 5 : Six products, the subtotal, the jitter, the total. The arithmetic on screen is the arithmetic that decided.
    Read the dissent : 5 : Who dissented, by how much, and the single strongest argument against the winner.
    Read the deciding axis : 4 : The axis whose weighted gap between winner and runner-up was largest.
  section Change the inputs
    Move one weight : 5 : Drag Bentham's rights from 0.20 to 0.60 and re-run at the same seed.
    Watch the verdict move : 5 : The winner changes, the margin narrows, and the trace shows which product moved.
  section Widen the view
    Scrub the chronicle: /chronicle : 4 : 32 eras; the alignment stack rebuilds as the year moves.
    Open the observatory: /observatory : 4 : Six towers, a coverage matrix over the six moral axes, and the gaps.
    Grind an experiment: /experiments/oracle-sweep : 3 : Sweep a driver and watch the metric respond monotonically.
    Look it up: /codex : 5 : 120 glossary terms, 28 canon texts, and the method that produced every number.
  section Leave unconvinced
    Disagree with a verdict : 5 : The reader's objection is the product working as intended; the trace exists so it can be located.
    Change the dataset instead : 4 : A dilemma proposal issue, or a PR against packages/seed. See docs/guides/contributing-guide.md.
